  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "A line saying that a blocking period ended stays on the steward's situation page forever, and in every steward brief. Background: the claim quota allows this machine one claimed goal at a time. A blocking period (an 'occurrence') is the stretch during which that held goal keeps ready priority-1 work waiting. Each period gets a start line and an end line in claim-quota.jsonl. When a period ends, the page now shows 'the occurrence ended: <goal> <cause>' in the program part's summary, and nothing ever removes that line. Each goal that ever ended a period adds one summary line, whether it is long concluded or was released last month. The only exception is a goal that is blocking again at that moment. The summary is the default view and is copied into every seat steward's brief. Within days of normal use (the brief's own receipts show two to three different holders in one day), the page and the agent's brief fill with closed history. That goes against D13's 'one line per occurrence' for current blocking and against the summary-by-default rule. The brief asks for the line to report that a period ended. It does not ask for that report to last forever.",
      "evidence": "Traced path at 0ad6a5689c. (1) claim_quota.go:117-138: readClaimQuotaOccurrences(root, ended) adds every end line in the file to the ended map, keyed by the ask id and holding the goal's name, with no age check. (2) claim_quota.go:140-150 appends to the file, and searching cmd and internal (excluding tests) finds no other writer and no pruning. (3) situation.go:666-671 turns every goal in ended into an Ended block unless open[held] is set (the goal is blocking again), the ledger tree is nil, or a current block exists for it. There is no time window and no 'ended at this tick' condition. (4) situation_compose.go:345-358 writes 'the occurrence ended: <held> <cause>' into program, and :383 adds program to the part's Summary. (5) seat_start.go:1150-1152 (pageFacts) appends every part's Summary to each seat brief. Example: holders A, B and C each block once on one day and their periods end. Every later page summary, and every later steward brief, then carries three 'the occurrence ended' lines, and one more for every future holder. The tests check only that the line appears within six ticks of the end (claim_quota_test.go:476), not that it ever goes away. Suggested correction: show an Ended block only for a period whose end line falls inside the page's recent window, or only until the next tick, or drop the summary line and keep the record. Then add a test showing the line is gone after a later end or after a later page read.",
